# MessageMonkey pagination

- Use the Audience → Connections pagination for every MessageMonkey list, report, gallery, history, and paginated picker, including new features.
- Server-rendered lists call `audiencePagination()` from `src/audience_pagination.php`; its shared template is `src/templates/audience/list-pagination.php`.
- Asynchronous lists use `renderAudiencePagination()` from `src/assets/js/audience-pagination.mjs`.
- Keep the same Items per page selector (10, 25, 50, 100), result range, Previous arrow, current page / total pages, and Next arrow. Use the shared `.mm-pagination` styles in `audience.css`.
- Preserve filters, sorting, account scope, and independent pagination parameters. Reset to page 1 when the page size changes, validate sizes on the server, and clamp page numbers to the current result count.
- Pagination owns the top separator. Mark paginated tables with `data-mm-paginated-table` so their final row and table/container bottom borders do not draw a second line.
- Do not introduce separate pagination markup, First/Last controls, page-number inputs, or incremental Show more controls in MessageMonkey.
- Verify multiple pages, empty results, first/last boundaries, filter retention, page-size changes, mobile layout, and both themes when changing pagination.
